<title>JAPAN: Aisin Seiki ask-only after factory fire.</title>
<headline>Aisin Seiki ask-only after factory fire.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Aisin Seiki Co Ltd were ask-only on Monday morning after a fire at its vehicle brake parts plant at the weekend, brokers said.</p>
<p>The shares were ask-only at 1,710 yen as of 0050 GMT, compared with Friday's close of 1,770 yen.  </p>
<p>Aisin Seiki said on Monday that the fire was likely to have caused 1.5 billion yen worth of damage to the facility based on book value.</p>
<p>The fire completely destroyed the factory, one of Aisin's 13 plants supplying vehicle parts to Toyota Motor Corp .</p>
<p>At 0156 GMT Aisin's share price stood at 1,680 yen, down 90 yen from Friday's close.</p>
</text>
